## Caching and consistency

Caching is optional. When enabled, document every cached value, its source of
truth, TTL/size bound, mutation path, and invalidation behavior. A multi-node
deployment must use persisted invalidation events plus scheduled replay so an
update on one node invalidates affected entries on every node. If the product
does not use caching, remove `backend/cache-management` with
`bash scripts/remove-cache-management.sh --apply` and state that explicitly.

